# Renova agent runtime entrypoint

Before editing or running the repository, read `AGENTS.md`. It is the single authoritative engineering instruction set. Then activate exactly one client adapter: `.agent/platforms/cursor.md`. It routes into `.agent/kickoff.md` and the shared `renova-product-engineering` skill layer.

The **host application is Cursor** even when Cursor is running a Claude, GPT, or another foundation model. Do not activate Claude Code, Codex, or ChatGPT/GPT adapters from the model name.

Canonical local sequence:

```bash
npm run dev -- doctor
npm run dev -- bootstrap
npm run dev
npm run dev -- check
npm run dev -- test-focused
npm run dev -- test-full
npm run dev -- stop
```

`env.local.example` / `.env.local` are local-development only. Never load `env.staging.example`, `backend/.env.staging.example`, or production examples into the canonical local runtime. Local green status is not staging/production evidence.
